TEXT -1600 0 Left 2 ;PSU - bench linear supply, tap-switched, 0..29 V / 2.5 A\n;Corrected version of psu.asc / psu.net.  Faults found in the original:\n;1. OVP compared VLOAD/11 against a divider of Vadj - but Vadj IS derived\n;from VLOAD, so both inputs had almost the same slope.  Nominal trip\n;came out at ~86 V, i.e. never; the comparator just sat in its linear\n;region.  Now referenced to the setpoint (VCTRL) instead.\n;2. That same OVP divider (R38, 10k) hung on the ADJ node and stole ~40 %\n;of the 5.68 mA programming current -> -25 % output error.\n;3. No latch: even if it had tripped, M4 would switch straight back on.\n;4. Current limit was a bare comparator driving Q6's base with no base\n;resistor and no compensation -> rail-to-rail chatter.\n;5. Bheat had a stray x100 -> Tj ran to 220 C and never came back.\n;6. R29 = 33R starved the 2N3055 bases (needs ~110 mA at 2.5 A).\n;7. Tap thresholds at 4.5 V / 14.5 V out against 17/35/53 V rails, i.e.\n;maximum dissipation exactly where it should have been minimum.\n;8. LM339 open-collector output tied through R48 to a node that sits at\n;VRAW+ (up to 55 V) - beyond its 36 V rating.  Q7 level shifts now.\n;9. M4 was an IRF4905 (55 V) on a rail that reaches 54 V no-load whenever\n;the breaker is off - 98 % of rating, on every power-down with the knob\n;up.  Now an IRF9540N (100 V); costs 0.23 V of drop, 0 V of margin.\n;10. A sustained short used to sit on the pass bank for 10.6 s waiting for\n;the heatsink to notice - at or past the derated SOA of a 2N3055.\n;Fixed the simple way: do not make the bank SURVIVE the fault, do not\n;let the fault LAST.  U15/U17 trip the existing latch after 300 ms of\n;sustained overcurrent.  Exposure 10.6 s -> 300 ms, which is inside the\n;2N3055 pulsed SOA with margin.  CC limit raised 2.5 -> 2.9 A so the\n;trip threshold (2.7 A) has room above the 2.4 A rated load.\n;Base stoppers are per-device (R29A/R29B) in case faster devices are\n;fitted later - fast devices in parallel can oscillate against each other.\n;Verified headless (LTspice -b).  See psu_test_fanfail.net for the OTP test.\n;NOTE: .lib paths are absolute because the CLI does not search the LTspice\n;library folder the way the GUI does.\n;MAINS + TAP-SWITCHED TRANSFORMER (3 x 18 Vpk secondaries in series)
TEXT 16 1296 Left 2 ;snubbers
TEXT 16 2576 Left 2 ;tap relays: U3 de-energised -> VACpos=N020 ; energised -> VACpos=N018 (3 windings)\n;U4 de-energised -> N020=N030 (1 winding) ; energised -> N020=N028 (2 windings)
TEXT 16 3216 Left 2 ;bridge + reservoir
TEXT 16 4176 Left 2 ;HOUSEKEEPING RAILS
TEXT 16 4816 Left 2 ;2.500 V reference
TEXT 16 5456 Left 2 ;-1.25 V rail so the output can be programmed down to 0 V
TEXT 16 6096 Left 2 ;TAP-CHANGE LOGIC  (thresholds set so VRAW+ tracks the setpoint)\n;Transformer fitted to the real one: 13.00 V rms open, 12.40 V into 8 ohm,\n;11.80 V into 4 ohm  (k=0.999, R13..R15=0.18 -> Rs = 0.40 ohm per winding).\n;Measured rail sag at 2.3 A with that fit:\n;tap1 min(VRAW+) = 12.65 V -> usable to 10.9 V out\n;tap2 min(VRAW+) = 27.28 V -> usable to 25.5 V out\n;tap3 min(VRAW+) = 41.89 V -> usable to 40.1 V out\n;so switch up at 9.2 V and 23.4 V out (3 V of guard band):\n;tap2 above VCTRL 1.59 , tap3 above VCTRL 4.04 (hysteresis ~2.1 V of output)\n;No-load tap3 rail is 52.9 V - that is what sizes M4, C6 and D16.
TEXT 16 8656 Left 2 ;SERIES DISCONNECT SWITCH M4 (the "electronic fuse" ahead of the pass bank)\n;Q7 level-shifts the 12 V comparator rail up to VRAW+ (up to 55 V)\n;FAULTn HIGH = healthy = M4 on.  FAULTn LOW = fault = M4 off.
TEXT 16 9616 Left 2 ;PASS BANK: LT317A + BD140 current-boost driving 2 x 2N3055\n;fed from PASS_IN (M4 drain), NOT from VRAW+ directly, so that turning M4 off\n;really does remove all power from the output - otherwise the LT317 keeps\n;feeding a shorted load and cooking after a thermal/OV shutdown
TEXT 16 10576 Left 2 ;resistencia de base INDIVIDUAL por dispositivo (antes una compartida de 10R):\n;frena oscilaciones parasitas entre transistores rapidos en paralelo
TEXT 16 11536 Left 2 ;per-device SOA backstop: steals base drive above ~1.4 A per 3055
TEXT 16 12176 Left 2 ;output network
TEXT 16 12816 Left 2 ;VOLTAGE PROGRAMMING\n;Vout = 1.25/220 * R17 = 5.6818 * V(VCTRL)      (R17 = 5 kohm pot)
TEXT 16 13456 Left 2 ;Cadj: soft-start + ripple rejection, with its ADJ->OUT protection diode
TEXT 16 14096 Left 2 ;(no second protection diode needed here: D15 across the pass bank already\n;clamps VLOAD to PASS_IN + 0.7 V, which is the OUT->IN protection)\n;CONSTANT-CURRENT LOOP  (2.5 A)\n;error amp output pulls ADJ down through D20; OR-ed with the CV loop
TEXT 16 15056 Left 2 ;R59+C12 = 1.5 ms integrator -> loop crosses over ~50 Hz, well under the\n;Cadj pole, so the limiter servos instead of chattering rail to rail
TEXT 16 15696 Left 2 ;QCC sinks ADJ current directly: its collector can sit at 28 V, so unlike a\n;diode-OR from a 12 V opamp it does not clamp the maximum output voltage
TEXT 16 16336 Left 2 ;OVER-VOLTAGE PROTECTION, REFERENCED TO THE SETPOINT, LATCHING\n;trip:  VLOAD > 1.10 * Vset + 2.0 V\n;latch: U9 inverts the trip and forces the sense node high for good\n;sense: VSENSE = 0.0476*VLOAD + 0.095   (R45 also carries the latch feedback)
TEXT 16 17296 Left 2 ;reference: VREF_OV = 0.296*VCTRL + 0.189  ->  trip at VLOAD = 6.21*VCTRL + 2.0
TEXT 16 17936 Left 2 ;22 us glitch filter: only a fault that persists latches
TEXT 16 18576 Left 2 ;POWER-ON RESET: U14 holds the latch released for ~50 ms after VCC appears.\n;(C17 is genuinely discharged at power-up -> the .ic below is physical, and\n;an RC has only one DC solution, so the start-up state is unambiguous.)
TEXT 16 19216 Left 2 ;latched fault also programs the output to 0 V (belt and braces)
TEXT 16 19856 Left 2 ;OVER-TEMPERATURE, wired-OR into the same latch (~89 C)
TEXT 16 20496 Left 2 ;DISPARO POR SOBRECORRIENTE SOSTENIDA  (disyuntor)\n;No intentamos que el banco AGUANTE la falta: no dejamos que dure.\n;carga nominal 2.4 A  <  disparo 2.7 A  <  limite CC 2.9 A\n;dispara el latch que ya existe (wired-OR sobre FAULTn, gratis).\n;Un pico corto de corriente no dispara; un corto de verdad, si.
TEXT 16 21776 Left 2 ;THERMAL MODEL + PROPORTIONAL FAN
TEXT 16 23056 Left 2 ;TEST STIMULUS\n;setpoint: 0 -> 5 V (= 0 -> 28.4 V out) between 0.5 s and 2.0 s\n;0.5-2.0 s  setpoint 0 -> 29 V          2.0-3.0 s  12 ohm (2.4 A)\n;3.0-3.15 s 2 ohm, 150 ms  -> CC limita y RECUPERA (bajo el umbral de 300 ms)\n;4.5-4.65 s corto franco 150 ms -> idem\n;5.2-5.6 s  consigna a 5.7 V           5.8 s  corto C-E de Q3 -> OVP enclava\n;El disparo por sobrecorriente sostenida se prueba en psu_test_short.net
TEXT 16 24960 Left 2 !K3 L3 L13 0.999
TEXT 16 25056 Left 2 !K4 L4 L14 0.999
TEXT 16 25152 Left 2 !K5 L5 L15 0.999
